{"base_rate":0.18811881188118812,"brier":0.0748869306930693,"bss":0.5096780616174583,"bss_hi":0.596220760567037,"bss_lo":0.40309502622984084,"chart":{"base":[224.6,105.0],"fp":[242.5,361.2],"lead":"62,246.7 272,223.3 482,192.2 692,125.7","note":{"base":"skill 0.51 — higher than 92% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end -3pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 45% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 1%; promised 67% → rained 69%"},"rel":"64.1,461.7 166.6,372.8 483.8,169.5"},"country":"TR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.017326732673267328,"ess":254.81288330896425,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Corum</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Corum rain forecast is strongly skilful, and honest except at one point on the scale.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (84%), believe about\n<b>85%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 505 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-18. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nCORUM, 0.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.51, ranked 18 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(5&ndash;53) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>301</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>20%</b></td><td class='num'>46</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>23%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>56</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>48</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>84%</td><td class='num'><b>85%</b></td><td class='num'>54</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">1 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Corum</b> <span class=\"muted\">Türkiye</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;19% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 19% of days.</p><p>The forecast did far better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">honest except at one point</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.51</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>5&ndash;53\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>505 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Corum &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Corum\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.199601328903654,378.3720930232558 88.62869565217392,318.69565217391306 139.92571428571426,258.5 227.99375000000003,154.5 354.5733333333333,44.96296296296293 354.5733333333333,112.37037037037038 227.99375000000003,260.6666666666667 139.92571428571426,336.5 88.62869565217392,374.0869565217391 59.199601328903654,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"313.5247524752475\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"313.5247524752475\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.199601328903654,378.3720930232558 88.62869565217392,310.7826086956522 139.92571428571426,297.5 227.99375000000003,200.0 354.5733333333333,71.92592592592592\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 301 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"59.199601328903654\" cy=\"378.3720930232558\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 20% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 46 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"88.62869565217392\" cy=\"310.7826086956522\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 23%&amp;#10;It rained 23% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 56 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"139.92571428571426\" cy=\"297.5\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 48%&amp;#10;It rained 50% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 48 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"227.99375000000003\" cy=\"200.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 84%&amp;#10;It rained 85% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 54 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"354.5733333333333\" cy=\"71.92592592592592\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(19%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">Not enough days in this city's record to split the year into four and still say anything defensible about each part. The split is shown only where it is supported.</p>\n"},"lat":40.54889,"lon":34.95333,"n":505,"n_cities":216,"name":"Corum","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.003388704318936877,"n":301,"obs":0.009966777408637873,"sig":false},{"hi":0.15,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.08652173913043479,"n":46,"obs":0.1956521739130435,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.15,"mean":0.2314285714285714,"n":56,"obs":0.23214285714285715,"sig":false},{"hi":0.65,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.4802083333333334,"n":48,"obs":0.5,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.65,"mean":0.8377777777777777,"n":54,"obs":0.8518518518518519,"sig":false}],"prcp_km":0.3,"provisional":false,"rank":18,"rank_hi":53.02499999999998,"rank_lo":5.0,"reliability":0.0011690818185831774,"resolution":0.07549014870648071,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"corum","station":"CORUM","timezone":"Europe/Istanbul"}